<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stanislaus Hosius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1504">1504</a>–<a href="/years/1579">1579</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Stanisław Hozjusz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stanislaus Hosius was a Polish churchman and theologian, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Warmia from 1551 and a cardinal from 1561. A leading figure of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/counter-reformation">Counter-Reformation</a>, he wrote a widely read defence of Catholic doctrine and presided as papal legate over the final sessions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-trent">Council of Trent</a>. In 1564 he brought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/braniewo">Braniewo</a>, founding their first college in the Polish lands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stanislaus-hosius.jpg" alt="Stanislaus Hosius" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marcello Bacciarelli · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stanis%C5%82aw_Hozjusz_1.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
